FUN_000446-T1	eggNOG-mapper	CDS	1	373	361.0	+	.	ID=FUN_000446-T1;em_target=104355.XP_007870414.1;em_score=361.0;em_evalue=4.93e-120;em_tcov=89.7;em_searcher=diamond;em_OGs=COG0258@1|root,KOG2519@2759|Eukaryota,38GN8@33154|Opisthokonta,3NUX0@4751|Fungi,3UYI3@5204|Basidiomycota,2286F@155619|Agaricomycetes,3H2P1@355688|Agaricomycetes incertae sedis;em_COG_cat=L;em_desc=Structure-specific nuclease with 5'-flap endonuclease and 5'-3' exonuclease activities involved in DNA replication and repair. During DNA replication, cleaves the 5'-overhanging flap structure that is generated by displacement synthesis when DNA polymerase encounters the 5'-end of a downstream Okazaki fragment. It enters the flap from the 5'-end and then tracks to cleave the flap base, leaving a nick for ligation. Also involved in the long patch base excision repair (LP-BER) pathway, by cleaving within the apurinic apyrimidinic (AP) site-terminated flap. Acts as a genome stabilization factor that prevents flaps from equilibrating into structurs that lead to duplications and deletions. Also possesses 5'-3' exonuclease activity on nicked or gapped double- stranded DNA, and exhibits RNase H activity. Also involved in replication and repair of rDNA and in repairing mitochondrial DNA;em_max_annot_lvl=4751|Fungi;em_Preferred_name=FEN1;em_PFAMs=XPG_I,XPG_N;em_KEGG_ko=ko:K04799;em_KEGG_Pathway=ko03030,ko03410,ko03450,map03030,map03410,map03450;em_BRITE=ko00000,ko00001,ko01000,ko03032,ko03400,ko04147;em_GOs=GO:0000003,GO:0000228,GO:0000278,GO:0000726,GO:0000731,GO:0000734,GO:0001302,GO:0003006,GO:0003674,GO:0003824,GO:0004518,GO:0004519,GO:0004520,GO:0004527,GO:0004529,GO:0004536,GO:0005575,GO:0005622,GO:0005623,GO:0005634,GO:0005657,GO:0005694,GO:0005737,GO:0005739,GO:0005829,GO:0006139,GO:0006259,GO:0006260,GO:0006261,GO:0006271,GO:0006273,GO:0006281,GO:0006284,GO:0006286,GO:0006302,GO:0006303,GO:0006310,GO:0006312,GO:0006401,GO:0006725,GO:0006793,GO:0006796,GO:0006807,GO:0006950,GO:0006974,GO:0006996,GO:000704